    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 14, 2026, is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him the clear centerpiece of today\u2019s lineup. Facing Buehler, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive +16% park factor and a +13% skill-based matchup projection, as his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching elevates his ceiling significantly. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.52) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.58) follow closely in the production hierarchy. **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly intriguing start; while his platoon splits are slightly negative, his score is bolstered by a favorable park and a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" green light against Rogers, which aligns perfectly with our organizational priority on stolen base efficiency. **Kyle Tucker** (68.08) remains a high-floor anchor despite a Neutral Platoon status, while **Andy Pages** (65.80) rounds out our top-tier grouping, benefiting from the same favorable baserunning environment as **Jackson Merrill**.\n\nConversely, the lineup construction faced a tight margin at the margins, with **Miguel Vargas** (43.55) narrowly missing the cut behind **Dominic Smith** (47.44) and **Wade Meckler** (45.25). While **Miguel Vargas** offers solid plate discipline, his matchup against Sheehan is penalized by a significant -15% SP skill adjustment, which pushed his efficiency just below the threshold for our final utility spot. We remain cautious with **Liam Hicks**, whose score of 41.15 is the lowest in the starting nine; while his leadoff status provides a nice +10% order boost, he is facing a genuine hurdle in Skenes, an elite arm with a 2.99 xERA. Owners should monitor the Skenes outing closely, as the high-strikeout nature of the opposing starter introduces a non-trivial risk to our daily AVG metrics. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** currently sidelined on the IL, the Waves are leaning heavily on the speed-oriented profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** to keep the SB category competitive despite the challenging pitching matchups ahead.",
